      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To find the annual straight-line depreciation, first calculate the depreciable cost by subtracting the salvage value from the initial cost: $45,000 - $5,000 = $40,000. Next, divide this depreciable cost by the useful life in years. Therefore, your annual straight-line depreciation is \\$40,000 / 8 years, which equals $5,000 per year.",
      "source": "target",
