      "content": "To find the book value at the end of year 3, first calculate the total accumulated depreciation over three years by multiplying the annual depreciation by three: $5,000 \\times 3 = \\$15,000$. Then, subtract this total accumulated depreciation from the original cost of the equipment. The book value at the end of year 3 will be $\\$45,000 - \\$15,000 = \\$30,000$.",
      "source": "target",
